  <!-- Architecture Section -->
  <section id="architecture" class="architecture-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span>ARCHITECTURE</span>
      <span class="heading-badge verified">FULL PRODUCTION ARCHITECTURE</span>
    </div>

    <div class="architecture-card">
      <div class="arch-badge-container">
        <span class="arch-tag">Current Verified Architecture (Day 1–Day 9)</span>
      </div>

      <pre class="architecture-diagram"><code>Internet
   │
   ▼
Application Load Balancer
   │
┌──┴────────────┐
▼               ▼
EC2-A           EC2-B
(us-east-1a)    (us-east-1b)
│               │
└──┬────────────┘
   ▼
Auto Scaling Group (Launch Template v2)
   │
   ▼
Private DB Subnets (us-east-1a / us-east-1b)
   │
   ▼
RDS MariaDB (TCP 3306 ← App SG Only)
   │
   ▼
CloudWatch Observability (Alarms • Metrics • Agent)</code></pre>

      <div class="architecture-explanations">
        <div class="arch-explain-item">
          <strong>Multi-AZ Load Distribution</strong>
          <p>The Application Load Balancer distributes incoming HTTP traffic evenly across compute instances spanning two Availability Zones (us-east-1a and us-east-1b).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-explain-item">
          <strong>Launch Template Consistency</strong>
          <p>EC2 instances are launched from a centralized Launch Template that defines the dynamic Ubuntu LTS AMI, security group, and bootstrap script.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-explain-item">
          <strong>Auto Scaling Capacity</strong>
          <p>The Auto Scaling Group maintains desired capacity (2 instances) across both Availability Zones and automatically replaces unhealthy or terminated instances.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-explain-item">
          <strong>Health-Based Traffic Routing</strong>
          <p>Continuous Target Group health checks against the <code>/health</code> endpoint determine whether instances receive user traffic, isolating degraded nodes automatically.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-explain-item">
          <strong>Isolated Database Tier</strong>
          <p>RDS MariaDB deployed across private database subnets with no internet route. Port 3306 ingress is strictly restricted to the EC2 Application Security Group.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-explain-item">
          <strong>Fleet Telemetry & Observability</strong>
          <p>CloudWatch Unified Agent monitors fleet CPU, memory, and disk metrics with automated threshold alarms routing notifications on latency or host degradation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


